{
  "_note": [
    "The local language and image-reading models of the platform, and where their",
    "weights come from. ONE table: the installer downloads from it, the ComfyUI",
    "client resolves an alias to a weights folder with it, the model lists of the",
    "settings page and the comparison surfaces are read off it.",
    "",
    "Keys are the platform's local aliases, the way the register",
    "(hardware_matrix.defaults.json) and the settings spell them without their",
    "'local/' prefix. 'repo' is the Hugging Face repository the weights are",
    "fetched from, verbatim; 'dir' is the folder under <ComfyUI>/models/llm/ the",
    "snapshot is written to, and the name ComfyUI's node lists. Every model is",
    "safetensors and is loaded by ComfyUI itself, under its memory management.",
    "",
    "One repository per alias. Where the maker publishes an FP8 checkpoint of a",
    "model above ~20 B parameters, that is the one (a 27 B model is 55.6 GB in",
    "BF16 and 30.9 GB in FP8); everything smaller is the BF16 release. size_gb",
    "is the sum of the safetensors files the download fetches, read off the",
    "repository on 2026-09-12. 'ignore' names files the download leaves out:",
    "Mistral ships each model twice, once for transformers and once",
    "'consolidated' for its own runtime. 'gated: true' means the maker asks",
    "for a Hugging Face account that accepted the model's licence; the download",
    "then needs HF_TOKEN. Loading an FP8 checkpoint needs accelerate in ComfyUI's",
    "venv (comfyui_nodes/ai4artsed_comfyui/requirements.txt).",
    "",
    "'vision' is a property of the checkpoint (it carries a vision tower);",
    "'chat_capable' is the platform's own decision which models are offered on",
    "the comparison surfaces, carried over from the GGUF registry unchanged.",
    "Every 'vision' flag was read off the repository's config.json (a",
    "vision_config entry) on 2026-09-12, except the three gated models, whose",
    "config is behind the licence gate and whose flag follows their model card."
  ],
